# Advisories that Trivy reports but that Nootle is not exposed to.
#
# Keep this file minimal and justified — every entry is a HIGH/CRITICAL finding
# the Security Scan would otherwise block on. Re-check an entry whenever the
# assumptions in its justification change.

# react-router: "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before 400 Response"
#
# Not applicable. The advisory requires React Router's RSC / Framework mode,
# where the router handles server requests and executes actions. Nootle is a
# Tauri desktop app: it uses declarative routing only (BrowserRouter + Routes
# in src/App.tsx), has no server, no React Server Components, and no router
# loaders or actions. There is no request path for the bypass to affect.
#
# It is also unreachable by upgrading: the fix landed in react-router 8.3.0,
# but react-router-dom has no 8.x line — v8 folded it into the react-router
# package — so clearing this requires migrating off react-router-dom rather
# than bumping a version.
#
# Revisit if Nootle ever adopts React Router's framework/RSC mode, or when the
# app migrates to react-router v8 (at which point this entry should be removed).
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
